  "title": "Breaking Changes & New Subscription Plan Transition APIs",
  "summary": "This update introduces breaking changes by making `packageName` and `token` strictly required in certain contexts and `transitionState` read-only. Developers can now programmatically manage subscription plan transitions with new `cancelplantransition` and `scheduleplantransition` methods.",
  "details": "Developers should be aware of several breaking changes: the `packageName` and `token` parameters are now strictly required in certain API calls, and the `transitionState` property within the `TransitionInfo` schema has become read-only. Ensure your integrations provide these required parameters and do not attempt to modify `transitionState`.\nAlongside these changes, the API gains powerful new capabilities for managing subscription plan transitions. Two new methods, `purchases.subscriptionsv2.cancelplantransition` and `purchases.subscriptionsv2.scheduleplantransition`, are now available. These allow you to programmatically cancel an in-progress plan transition or schedule a future one. Supporting schemas like `PlanTransitionDetails`, `TransitionInfo`, `DefiniteTransition`, and `TentativeTransition` have been added to facilitate these operations, providing granular control over subscription lifecycle management.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
